# Code Owners for paths that publish to S3.
#
# This file auto-requests reviewers on PRs that touch the listed paths. To
# ENFORCE that the listed reviewer must approve before merge (vs just being
# tagged), enable a branch protection rule in the GitHub UI:
#   Settings → Branches → master → "Require pull request reviews" + "Require
#   review from Code Owners".
#
# The branch-per-env publish workflow means a merge to master triggers a
# publish to prod S3 — same with merges to develop/qa. CODEOWNERS guards prod
# by gating merges to master; we deliberately don't gate develop/qa to keep
# iteration fast.

# Anything that produces what gets shipped to candidates.
# Reviewer is the engineering team — any gp-eng member can approve a merge to
# master / push to prod S3. (Per-person ownership creates a single point of
# blocking review.)
packages/runbooks/experiments/                                @thegoodparty/gp-eng
packages/runbooks/scripts/python/publish_experiments.py       @thegoodparty/gp-eng
packages/runbooks/scripts/python/test_experiment_manifests.py @thegoodparty/gp-eng
.github/workflows/publish-experiments.yml                     @thegoodparty/gp-eng
.github/CODEOWNERS                                            @thegoodparty/gp-eng
